      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:07:16Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the official SpankChain post-mortem, exploit and deployment transactions, verified LedgerChannel source, archive-node runtime at deployment block 6239908 and immediately before exploit block 6467248, and the commit-pinned reproduction. In the anchor transaction the attacker supplies 5 ETH, the malicious token callback re-enters LCOpenTimeout, LedgerChannel makes thirty-two 5 ETH withdrawals before deleting the channel, and the attack contract forwards 160 ETH to the attacker. The vulnerable ordering is in LedgerChannel itself. It is a direct contract rather than a proxy: the DELEGATECALL instructions in its verified runtime target the ECTools address statically linked at deployment, and the exploit path does not execute them. The 17,133-byte runtime has hash 0x46a8b25053a9cf565e3032a4e9348281eda7cc5f3837a3613aea7a3dd9b9d3c2 at both historical blocks, establishing deployment as the applicable code-selection event. The protocol's own report aggregates 165.38 ETH stolen and about $4,000 of BOOTY immobilized across the incident."
    }
  ],
